\subsection{Solver Strategy and Sparsity Exploitation}
\label{subsec:solver_strategy}

The preferred time integrators for this framework are $L$-stable implicit Rosenbrock and stiff SDIRK methods, specifically the \texttt{Rodas5P} engine within the SciML ecosystem \citep{rackauckas2017sciml}. \texttt{Rodas5P} handles fast transient decay along the TKE coordinate while advancing the slow rotational and thermodynamic variables with large, adaptive time steps.

Because vertical spatial operators are discretized using localized central differences, coupling is restricted to adjacent grid nodes ($i-1, i, i+1$). The solver maps this structural constraint directly to a \texttt{BandedMatrix} Jacobian prototype. Combining this band structure with matrix coloring vectors decouples automatic differentiation updates from vertical grid scaling, reducing linear system solver overhead from $\mathcal{O}(N^3)$ matrix inversions to an $\mathcal{O}(N)$ routine per timestep.

\subsection{Implementation Contract for Code Generation and Reproducibility}
\label{subsec:ai_impl_contract}

To maintain strict programmatic reproducibility in single-column code generation, this section defines the implementation template contract. All model extensions must strictly adhere to these variable mappings and structural constraints.

\paragraph{Mathematical-to-Code Identifier Mapping.}
State variables map directly to internal identifiers within the spatial differential operator loop:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Zonal momentum $U$ maps to \texttt{U},
    \item Meridional momentum $V$ maps to \texttt{V},
    \item Potential temperature $\theta$ maps to \texttt{theta},
    \item Surface skin temperature $T_s$ maps to \texttt{Ts},
    \item Fast TKE coordinate $e$ maps to closure diagnostics used to compute face diffusivities.
\end{itemize}

\paragraph{Interleaved Block State Layout.}
To optimize matrix coloring and vector cache alignment, the multi-layer SCM state vector is stored in a block-interleaved layout:
\begin{equation}
\mathbf{X} = [T_s, U_1, V_1, \theta_1, U_2, V_2, \theta_2, \dots, U_N, V_N, \theta_N]^T.
\label{eq:state_layout_interleaved}
\end{equation}
Vertical diffusive transport maps to a 3-point stencil on a staggered vertical grid ($\Delta z = 2\,\mathrm{m}$), enforcing a strictly banded Jacobian profile.

\paragraph{Runtime Scale Height Clamping.}
The non-local emergent scale height is clamped explicitly at runtime to prevent unphysical boundary-layer extensions under strong stratification:
\begin{equation}
h_{\mathrm{eff}} = \max\left(h_{\min},\, \min\left(h_{\mathrm{diagnosed}},\, h_{\max}\right)\right),
\label{eq:nonlocal_h_clamp}
\end{equation}
with default bounds set to $h_{\min} = \SBLParamNonlocalHMin\,\mathrm{m}$ and $h_{\max} = \SBLParamNonlocalHMax\,\mathrm{m}$.

\paragraph{Type-Generic Automatic Differentiation Contract.}
To support colored forward-mode AD via \texttt{ForwardDiff.jl}, internal flux routines, boundary face buffers, and intermediate diagnostic arrays must remain type-generic. Memory buffers must instantiate dynamically to accept either \texttt{Float64} or dual-valued types (\texttt{ForwardDiff.Dual}), avoiding scalar type-casting that disrupts dual-number propagation.

\paragraph{Physical Temperature Safeguard Floor.}
To maintain longwave radiative equilibrium ($\sigma T_s^4$) and stable surface energy closure under clear-sky polar cooling, surface skin temperature is protected by an explicit physical lower bound:
\begin{equation}
T_{s,\min} = 220\,\mathrm{K}.
\label{eq:ts_physical_floor}
\end{equation}

\subsection{Numerical Workflow and Julia Code Reference}
\label{subsec:numerical_workflow}

The complete computational pipeline is concise: state vectors are constructed, fast--slow residuals are evaluated in a single right-hand side function, and the stiff solver advances the system across collapse and recovery cycles.

A complete Julia reference implementation of the gated $4\text{D}$ GSPT system is provided below, leveraging the SciML \texttt{DifferentialEquations.jl} stack with forward-mode automatic differentiation:

\begingroup
\footnotesize
\begin{verbatim}
using DifferentialEquations
using LinearAlgebra
using ForwardDiff

# ====================================================================
# 1. Physical and Numerical Parameters (Active Baseline)
# ====================================================================
const Ug        = {{param_u_g_code}}          # Zonal geostrophic wind (m/s)
const Vg        = {{param_v_g_code}}          # Meridional geostrophic wind (m/s)
const Ta        = {{param_t_a_code}}          # Reference air temperature (K)
const Tdeep     = {{param_t_deep_code}}       # Deep soil/ice core temperature (K)
const Rdown     = {{param_r_down_code}}       # Downward longwave radiation (W/m^2)
const f_cor     = {{param_f_coriolis_code}}   # Coriolis parameter (s^-1)

const epsilon   = {{param_epsilon_code}}      # Fast-slow timescale ratio (eps << 1)
const delta     = {{param_delta_code}}        # Background TKE floor (m^2/s^2)
const K_buoy    = {{param_k_code}}            # Buoyant destruction scale (m/s^2)
const beta      = {{param_beta_code}}         # Stability sensitivity parameter
const h_bl      = {{param_h_code}}            # Boundary layer bulk scale height (m)
const h_min     = 20.0          # Lower bound for emergent h_eff (m)
const h_max     = 400.0         # Upper bound for emergent h_eff (m)
const l0        = {{param_l0_code}}           # Master turbulent mixing length (m)
const gamma     = 1.4e-3        # Effective momentum drag scaling (s^-1)
const CH        = 1.2e-3        # Thermal exchange coefficient
const eta       = 1.5           # Shear production efficiency

const sigma_SB  = {{param_sigma_sb_code}}     # Stefan-Boltzmann constant (W/m^2/K^4)
const lambda    = {{param_lambda_soil_code}}  # Soil/Ice thermal conductivity (W/m/K)
const d_soil    = {{param_d_soil_code}}       # Soil coupling depth (m)
const rho_cp    = {{param_rho_cp_code}}       # Volumetric heat capacity of air (J/m^3/K)
const C_skin    = {{param_c_skin_code}}       # Thermal capacity of skin layer (J/m^2/K)

# Numerical Safeguard Parameters
const alpha_safe = 1.0e-6      # Damping scale for the safeguard floor gate
const ts_min     = 220.0       # Validated physical Arctic surface floor (K)

# ====================================================================
# 2. Vector Field Definition (AD-Safe, Type-Generic Structure)
# ====================================================================
function gspt_sbl_dynamics!(dx, x, p, t)
    # State mapping: x = [e, U, V, Ts]
    e  = x[1]
    U  = x[2]
    V  = x[3]
    Ts = max(x[4], ts_min) # Apply physical safety floor inline

    # Shifted TKE coordinate
    phi = e + delta

    # Emergent effective boundary-layer height with runtime clamp
    vel_ratio = sqrt(U^2 + V^2 + 1.0e-6) / max(Ug, 1.0e-6)
    h_eff = clamp(h_bl * vel_ratio, h_min, h_max)
    gamma_eff = gamma * (h_bl / h_eff)

    # 2.1 Smooth Safeguard Floor Gate
    # +1.0e-15 prevents NaN dual-number derivatives
    # from the 1/(2*sqrt(phi)) singular limit at phi = 0.
    psi = sqrt(phi + 1.0e-15) / (sqrt(phi + 1.0e-15) + alpha_safe)

    # 2.2 Physical Auxiliary Functions
    # Bounded tanh stability response prevents runaway buoyancy growth
    G_Ts = tanh(beta * (Ta - Ts) / Ta)

    # Net mechanical production minus buoyancy balance
    shear_prod = eta * gamma_eff * (U^2 + V^2)
    buoy_dest  = K_buoy * G_Ts
    Delta      = shear_prod - buoy_dest

    # C^inf coordinate shifting avoids non-differentiable max() gates
    # and prevents derivative blowup in ForwardDiff.Dual components
    sqrt_phi_reg = sqrt(phi + 1.0e-15)

    # Surface Energy Budget Terms
    Rn = Rdown - sigma_SB * (Ts^4)
    H  = rho_cp * CH * sqrt_phi_reg * (Ts - Ta)
    G  = lambda * (Ts - Tdeep) / d_soil

    # 2.3 Evaluated Tendencies
    # Fast TKE Equation: activated production + non-linear dissipation
    dx[1] = (1.0 / epsilon) * (l0 * Delta * phi * psi + beta * phi - (phi^(3/2)) / l0)

    # Slow Momentum and Thermodynamic Equations
    dx[2] = f_cor * (V - Vg) - gamma_eff * sqrt_phi_reg * U
    dx[3] = -f_cor * (U - Ug) - gamma_eff * sqrt_phi_reg * V
    dx[4] = (1.0 / C_skin) * (Rn - H - G)

    return nothing
end

# ====================================================================
# 3. Solver Execution and Integration Setup
# ====================================================================
# Initial Conditions: Cold active Arctic boundary layer
x0 = [0.05, 5.0, -1.0, 250.0]
tspan = (0.0, 43200.0) # Full 12-hour production window

prob = ODEProblem(gspt_sbl_dynamics!, x0, tspan)

# Solve using Rodas5P (5th order A-L-stable Rosenbrock method with AD)
sol = solve(prob, Rodas5P(autodiff=true), reltol=1.0e-6, abstol=1.0e-8)
\end{verbatim}
